# Declaring a 2nd Major or Degree

## What is the difference between a 2nd Major or Degree?

A 2nd major is when you declare another major within your own college(ie Mechanical Engineering), while a 2nd degree is when you declare another major outside your own college(ie Math). Double majors graduate within grainger with both major apperaing on your diploma while Double degrees graduate with 2 diplomas, one from grainger and the other one from wherever the college that your 2nd major outside of grainger is under.

## Should I Declare a 2nd Major or Degree?
Taking on an additional program of study like a 2nd Major or Degree will always be relatively heavy, as majors within graingers do not have high levels of overlap and is incredibly difficult, while majors outside of grainger is subjected to an additional 30 credit hours of non-overlapping courses as detailed below. Classes for 2nd major or degree may or may not count towards classes for your major, be it core courses or free electives, so keep this in mind when making your decision as it will either only lightly or greatly increase your workload. (Get some double major graduates as I am no where near graduating yet). It also counts for James Schoalrs plan or contract.

Having a lot of carried in credits or completion of proficiency exams of important introductory classes is almost a requirement in order to keep most courseloads within reasonable levels. You are limited within 10 semesters to complete required courses for both majors so plan accordingly.

## How do I Declare a 2nd Major or Degree?
For both 2nd Major and Degree, it is best that you communicate with your course advisors for course planning and communication across majors or degrees. Careful planning is required in order to fullfil requirements for both major or degree while keeping graduation times under 4 to 5 years. You will also need to fill out multiple forms for applications(for LAS, this is a double degree declaration form), as well as completing transfer requirements for your specific 2nd major or degree. For 2nd degrees, you also have to contact the department head of the college that your 2nd major is under. Submission of all materials is required no later than 1 month prior before your last semester.

Majors with significant overlaps are not allowed, meaning that CE major students cannot declare EE as their 2nd major and vice versa.

Additional Requirements:
- GPA above 3.0
- 12 hrs of distinct advanced level courses(300-400 level courses, cannot overlap, different colleges may have different categorizations of advanced level courses)
- (For Double Degrees only) 30 extra credit hours that is not counted for the first degree

## Taking Classes for your 2nd Major or Degree

While the introductory courses are likely to be restricted while you have yet to declare your 2nd major or degree, you are considered a student under the 2nd Major or degree once the transfer process are completed and as such are not limited to course restrictions as minors do. As such, it is best to declare your 2nd Major or Degree early on in order to avoid course registration limitaions

